IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc22-pleas.l4 -- sections 606 to 619 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XX: pleas; special pleas; autrefois acquit and autrefois convict; libel; plea of not guilty). Part agent ccc22. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (the text's own words bring the case within the rule); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Tags in the comments: [M-a] a failed "if"/"where" or a flat negative counted as the text's no; [M-b] a prohibition or grant limited by its own wording counted as NOT the text's no (NOTHING);
-- [F:...] a fork line for NOTES.md (may-if, may-where, entitled, duty, unless). Section 2 terms and other parts' answers are INPUTS named for their section.

§ `Section 606 -- Pleas permitted`

-- src:12807 | 606 (1) An accused who is called on to plead may plead guilty or not guilty, or the special pleas authorized by this Part and no others.
@ref s 606(1) (src:12807-12807)
DECLARE `s 606(1) the plea` IS ONE OF
    `s 606(1) guilty`
    `s 606(1) not guilty`
    `s 606(1) autrefois acquit`
    `s 606(1) autrefois convict`
    `s 606(1) pardon`
    `s 606(1) an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act`
    `s 606(1) justification of a defamatory libel under section 611`
    `s 606(1) some other plea`

-- src:12807 | 606 (1) An accused who is called on to plead may plead guilty or not guilty, or the special pleas authorized by this Part and no others.
@ref s 606(1) (src:12807-12807)
GIVEN `the accused is called on to plead` IS A BOOLEAN
      plea IS A `s 606(1) the plea`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(1) the accused may enter the plea` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is called on to plead` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who is called on to plead"
        IF plea EQUALS `s 606(1) some other plea` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may plead guilty or not guilty, or the special pleas authorized by this Part and no others" [M-a]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (1.1): "only if": every condition must be satisfied. The conditions are necessary; the text does not say they are all that the court weighs.
-- src:12809 | (1.1) A court may accept a plea of guilty only if it is satisfied that
-- src:12810 | (a) the accused is making the plea voluntarily;
-- src:12811 | (b) the accused understands
-- src:12812 | (i) that the plea is an admission of the essential elements of the offence,
-- src:12813 | (ii) the nature and consequences of the plea, and
-- src:12814 | (iii) that the court is not bound by any agreement made between the accused and the prosecutor; and
-- src:12815 | (c) the facts support the charge.
@ref s 606(1.1) (src:12809-12815)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the accused is making the plea voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the accused understands that the plea is an admission of the essential elements of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the accused understands the nature and consequences of the plea` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the accused understands that the court is not bound by any agreement made between the accused and the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the facts support the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(1.1) the court may accept a plea of guilty` MEANS
    IF     `the court is satisfied that the accused is making the plea voluntarily`
       AND `the court is satisfied that the accused understands that the plea is an admission of the essential elements of the offence`
       AND `the court is satisfied that the accused understands the nature and consequences of the plea`
       AND `the court is satisfied that the accused understands that the court is not bound by any agreement made between the accused and the prosecutor`
       AND `the court is satisfied that the facts support the charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court may accept a plea of guilty only if it is satisfied that" [M-a]

-- src:12817 | (1.2) The failure of the court to fully inquire whether the conditions set out in subsection (1.1) are met does not affect the validity of the plea.
@ref s 606(1.2) (src:12817-12817)
GIVEN `the court failed to fully inquire whether the conditions set out in subsection (1.1) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(1.2) the court’s failure to inquire affects the validity of the plea` MEANS
    IF `the court failed to fully inquire whether the conditions set out in subsection (1.1) are met`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The failure of the court to fully inquire whether the conditions set out in subsection (1.1) are met does not affect the validity of the plea" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The failure of the court to fully inquire"

-- src:12819 | (2) Where an accused refuses to plead or does not answer directly, the court shall order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty.
@ref s 606(2) (src:12819-12819)
GIVEN `the accused refuses to plead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused does not answer directly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(2) the court must order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty` MEANS
    IF `the accused refuses to plead` OR `the accused does not answer directly`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused refuses to plead or does not answer directly, the court shall order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12819 | (2) Where an accused refuses to plead or does not answer directly, the court shall order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty.
@ref s 606(2) (src:12819-12819)
DECLARE `s 606(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 606(2) order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty`

@ref s 606(2) (src:12819-12819)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 606(2) action`
`s 606(2) the court must order the clerk to enter a plea of not guilty` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 606(2) order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the accused refused to plead or did not answer directly and the court did not order the clerk of the court to enter a plea of not guilty"

-- (3): "An accused is not entitled as of right to have his trial postponed": a flat negative (the answer is whether the accused is entitled as of right).
-- src:12821 | (3) An accused is not entitled as of right to have his trial postponed but the court may, if it considers that the accused should be allowed further time to plead, move to quash or prepare for his defence or for any other reason, adjourn the trial to a later time in the session or sittings of the court, or to the next of any subsequent session or sittings of the court, on such terms as the court considers proper.
@ref s 606(3) (src:12821-12821)
GIVEN `the accused asks for the trial to be postponed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(3) the accused is entitled as of right to have the trial postponed` MEANS
    IF `the accused asks for the trial to be postponed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An accused is not entitled as of right to have his trial postponed" [F:entitled] [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to have his trial postponed"

-- src:12821 | (3) An accused is not entitled as of right to have his trial postponed but the court may, if it considers that the accused should be allowed further time to plead, move to quash or prepare for his defence or for any other reason, adjourn the trial to a later time in the session or sittings of the court, or to the next of any subsequent session or sittings of the court, on such terms as the court considers proper.
@ref s 606(3) (src:12821-12821)
GIVEN `the court considers that the accused should be allowed further time to plead, move to quash or prepare for their defence, or for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(3) the court may adjourn the trial to a later time in the session or sittings, or to the next of any subsequent session or sittings` MEANS
    IF `the court considers that the accused should be allowed further time to plead, move to quash or prepare for their defence, or for any other reason`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it considers that the accused should be allowed further time to plead, move to quash or prepare for his defence or for any other reason" [F:may-if]

-- src:12823 | (4) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, where an accused or defendant pleads not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction, whether or not it is an included offence, the court may, with the consent of the prosecutor, accept that plea of guilty and, if the plea is accepted, the court shall find the accused or defendant not guilty of the offence charged and find him guilty of the offence in respect of which the plea of guilty was accepted and enter those findings in the record of the court.
@ref s 606(4) (src:12823-12823)
GIVEN `the accused pleads not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction, whether or not it is an included offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4) the court may accept the plea of guilty of the other offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused pleads not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction, whether or not it is an included offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an accused or defendant pleads not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction" [F:may-where] [M-a]
        IF NOT `the prosecutor consents` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, with the consent of the prosecutor, accept that plea of guilty"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12823 | (4) Notwithstanding any other provision of this Act, where an accused or defendant pleads not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction, whether or not it is an included offence, the court may, with the consent of the prosecutor, accept that plea of guilty and, if the plea is accepted, the court shall find the accused or defendant not guilty of the offence charged and find him guilty of the offence in respect of which the plea of guilty was accepted and enter those findings in the record of the court.
@ref s 606(4) (src:12823-12823)
GIVEN `the plea of guilty of the other offence is accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4) the court must find the accused not guilty of the offence charged, find the accused guilty of the other offence and enter the findings in the record` MEANS
    IF `the plea of guilty of the other offence is accepted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the plea is accepted, the court shall find the accused or defendant not guilty of the offence charged and find him guilty of the offence in respect of which the plea of guilty was accepted" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12825 | (4.1) If the accused is charged with a serious personal injury offence, as that expression is defined in section 752, or with the offence of murder, and the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement under which the accused will enter a plea of guilty of the offence charged — or a plea of not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction, whether or not it is an included offence — the court shall, after accepting the plea of guilty, inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement.
@ref s 606(4.1) (src:12825-12825)
GIVEN `s 752 the offence is a serious personal injury offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is the offence of murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement under which the accused will enter a plea of guilty of the offence charged, or a plea of not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has accepted the plea of guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the offence is the offence of murder` OR `s 752 the offence is a serious personal injury offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            (IF `the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement under which the accused will enter a plea of guilty of the offence charged, or a plea of not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction` AND `the court has accepted the plea of guilty`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement under which the accused will enter a plea of guilty of the offence charged" (the "If" fails) [M-a] [F:duty]
        IF `s 752 the offence is a serious personal injury offence` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a serious personal injury offence is for section 752, another part
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused is charged with a serious personal injury offence, as that expression is defined in section 752, or with the offence of murder" (neither) [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12825 | (4.1) If the accused is charged with a serious personal injury offence, as that expression is defined in section 752, or with the offence of murder, and the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement under which the accused will enter a plea of guilty of the offence charged — or a plea of not guilty of the offence charged but guilty of any other offence arising out of the same transaction, whether or not it is an included offence — the court shall, after accepting the plea of guilty, inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement.
@ref s 606(4.1) (src:12825-12825)
DECLARE `s 606(4.1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 606(4.1) inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement`

@ref s 606(4.1) (src:12825-12825)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 606(4.1) action`
`s 606(4.1) the court must inquire of the prosecutor after accepting the plea of guilty` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 606(4.1) inquire of the prosecutor if reasonable steps were taken to inform the victims of the agreement`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the court did not inquire of the prosecutor after accepting the plea of guilty"

-- (4.2): the five-years test is a helper over the core's Imprisonment. "Five years less a day" is below five years.
-- src:12827 | (4.2) If the accused is charged with an offence, as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Victims Bill of Rights, that is an indictable offence for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more, and that is not an offence referred to in subsection (4.1), and the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement referred to in subsection (4.1), the court shall, after accepting the plea of guilty, inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed if such an agreement were entered into, and, if so, whether reasonable steps were taken to inform that victim of the agreement.
@ref s 606(4.2) (src:12827-12827)
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment for the offence` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment for the offence`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN
        BRANCH
            IF term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months GREATER THAN 60 THEN JUST TRUE
            IF term's years TIMES 12 PLUS term's months EQUALS 60 AND (NOT term's `less a day`) THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more" (a shorter term, or five years less a day)
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the limb states no imprisonment

-- src:12827 | (4.2) If the accused is charged with an offence, as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Victims Bill of Rights, that is an indictable offence for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more, and that is not an offence referred to in subsection (4.1), and the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement referred to in subsection (4.1), the court shall, after accepting the plea of guilty, inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed if such an agreement were entered into, and, if so, whether reasonable steps were taken to inform that victim of the agreement.
@ref s 606(4.2) (src:12827-12827)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Victims Bill of Rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class of the offence` IS A `Class of offence`
      `the answer of s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is an offence referred to in subsection (4.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement referred to in subsection (4.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has accepted the plea of guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4.2) the court must inquire of the prosecutor whether any of the victims had advised the prosecutor of their desire to be informed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence's limb states no maximum imprisonment
        IF     `the offence is an offence as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Victims Bill of Rights`
           AND (`the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence` OR `the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`)
           AND `the answer of s 606(4.2) the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (NOT `the offence is an offence referred to in subsection (4.1)`)
           AND `the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement referred to in subsection (4.1)`
           AND `the court has accepted the plea of guilty`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused is charged with an offence, as defined in section 2 of the Canadian Victims Bill of Rights, that is an indictable offence for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more, and that is not an offence referred to in subsection (4.1), and the accused and the prosecutor have entered into an agreement referred to in subsection (4.1), the court shall" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- (4.3): if (4.1) or (4.2) applies and any victim was not informed before the plea was accepted, the prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible, take reasonable steps to inform the victim. For a victim who is dead or incapable, section 2.2 says who may act on their behalf for the purposes of section 606.
-- src:12829 | (4.3) If subsection (4.1) or (4.2) applies, and any victim was not informed of the agreement before the plea of guilty was accepted, the prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible, take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea.
@ref s 606(4.3) (src:12829-12829)
GIVEN `subsection (4.1) or (4.2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is dead or incapable of acting on their own behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim was informed of the agreement before the plea of guilty was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that individual was informed of the agreement before the plea of guilty was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `subsection (4.1) or (4.2) applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If subsection (4.1) or (4.2) applies" [M-a] [F:duty]
        IF `the victim was informed of the agreement before the plea of guilty was accepted` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and any victim was not informed of the agreement before the plea of guilty was accepted" [M-a] [F:duty]
        IF `the victim is dead or incapable of acting on their own behalf` AND `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the individual may act on the victim’s behalf is for section 2.2
        IF `the victim is dead or incapable of acting on their own behalf` AND `s 2.2 the individual may act on the victim’s behalf, subject to subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `that individual was informed of the agreement before the plea of guilty was accepted` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and any victim was not informed of the agreement" (the individual who may act on the victim’s behalf under section 2.2 was informed) [M-a] [F:duty]
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12829 | (4.3) If subsection (4.1) or (4.2) applies, and any victim was not informed of the agreement before the plea of guilty was accepted, the prosecutor shall, as soon as feasible, take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea.
@ref s 606(4.3) (src:12829-12829)
DECLARE `s 606(4.3) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 606(4.3) take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea`

@ref s 606(4.3) (src:12829-12829)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 606(4.3) action`
`s 606(4.3) the prosecutor must inform the victim as soon as feasible` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 606(4.3) take reasonable steps to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the prosecutor did not take reasonable steps, as soon as feasible, to inform the victim of the agreement and the acceptance of the plea"

-- src:12831 | (4.4) Neither the failure of the court to inquire of the prosecutor, nor the failure of the prosecutor to take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the agreement, affects the validity of the plea.
@ref s 606(4.4) (src:12831-12831)
GIVEN `the court failed to inquire of the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor failed to take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 606(4.4) the failure affects the validity of the plea` MEANS
    IF `the court failed to inquire of the prosecutor` OR `the prosecutor failed to take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the agreement`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Neither the failure of the court to inquire of the prosecutor, nor the failure of the prosecutor to take reasonable steps to inform the victims of the agreement, affects the validity of the plea" [M-a]
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Neither the failure of the court to inquire of the prosecutor, nor the failure of the prosecutor to take reasonable steps"

-- src:12832 | (5) [Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 37]
@ref s 606(5) (repealed) (src:12832-12832)
`s 606(5) what the text shows` MEANS "[Repealed, 2022, c. 17, s. 37]"

§ `Section 607 -- Special pleas`

-- src:12834 | 607 (1) An accused may plead the special pleas of
-- src:12835 | (a) autrefois acquit;
-- src:12836 | (b) autrefois convict;
-- src:12837 | (c) pardon; and
-- src:12838 | (d) an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act.
@ref s 607(1) (src:12834-12838)
GIVEN plea IS A `s 606(1) the plea`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(1) the accused may plead the special plea` MEANS
    IF plea EQUALS `s 606(1) autrefois acquit` OR plea EQUALS `s 606(1) autrefois convict` OR plea EQUALS `s 606(1) pardon` OR plea EQUALS `s 606(1) an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "An accused may plead the special pleas of (a) autrefois acquit; (b) autrefois convict; (c) pardon; and (d) an expungement order" (other special pleas are in other sections, such as section 611)

-- src:12840 | (2) An accused who is charged with defamatory libel may plead in accordance with sections 611 and 612.
@ref s 607(2) (src:12840-12840)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with defamatory libel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(2) the accused may plead in accordance with sections 611 and 612` MEANS
    IF `the accused is charged with defamatory libel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who is charged with defamatory libel"

-- src:12842 | (3) The pleas of autrefois acquit, autrefois convict, pardon and an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act shall be disposed of by the judge without a jury before the accused is called on to plead further.
@ref s 607(3) (src:12842-12842)
GIVEN plea IS A `s 606(1) the plea`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(3) the plea must be disposed of by the judge without a jury before the accused is called on to plead further` MEANS
    IF plea EQUALS `s 606(1) autrefois acquit` OR plea EQUALS `s 606(1) autrefois convict` OR plea EQUALS `s 606(1) pardon` OR plea EQUALS `s 606(1) an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The pleas of autrefois acquit, autrefois convict, pardon and an expungement order"

-- src:12844 | (4) When the pleas referred to in subsection (3) are disposed of against the accused, he may plead guilty or not guilty.
@ref s 607(4) (src:12844-12844)
GIVEN `the pleas referred to in subsection (3) are disposed of against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(4) the accused may plead guilty or not guilty` MEANS
    IF `the pleas referred to in subsection (3) are disposed of against the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the pleas referred to in subsection (3) are disposed of against the accused, he may plead guilty or not guilty" [F:may-where] [M-a]

-- src:12846 | (5) Where an accused pleads autrefois acquit or autrefois convict, it is sufficient if he
-- src:12847 | (a) states that he has been lawfully acquitted, convicted or discharged under subsection 730(1), as the case may be, of the offence charged in the count to which the plea relates; and
-- src:12848 | (b) indicates the time and place of the acquittal, conviction or discharge under subsection 730(1).
@ref s 607(5) (src:12846-12848)
GIVEN `the accused pleads autrefois acquit or autrefois convict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused states that they have been lawfully acquitted, convicted or discharged under subsection 730(1), as the case may be, of the offence charged in the count to which the plea relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused indicates the time and place of the acquittal, conviction or discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(5) the accused’s statement of the plea is sufficient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused pleads autrefois acquit or autrefois convict` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an accused pleads autrefois acquit or autrefois convict"
        IF `the accused states that they have been lawfully acquitted, convicted or discharged under subsection 730(1), as the case may be, of the offence charged in the count to which the plea relates` AND `the accused indicates the time and place of the acquittal, conviction or discharge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is sufficient if he (a) states that he has been lawfully acquitted, convicted or discharged under subsection 730(1) ...; and (b) indicates the time and place" [M-a]

-- (6): the BAR: JUST TRUE where the subsection bars the plea of autrefois convict.
-- src:12850 | (6) A person who is alleged to have committed an act or omission outside Canada that is an offence in Canada by virtue of any of subsections 7(2) to (3.1) or (3.7), or an offence under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act, and in respect of which the person has been tried and convicted outside Canada, may not plead autrefois convict with respect to a count that charges that offence if
-- src:12851 | (a) at the trial outside Canada the person was not present and was not represented by counsel acting under the person’s instructions, and
-- src:12852 | (b) the person was not punished in accordance with the sentence imposed on conviction in respect of the act or omission,
-- src:12853 | notwithstanding that the person is deemed by virtue of subsection 7(6), or subsection 12(1) of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act, as the case may be, to have been tried and convicted in Canada in respect of the act or omission.
@ref s 607(6) (src:12850-12853)
GIVEN `the offence is an offence in Canada by virtue of any of subsections 7(2) to (3.1) or (3.7), or an offence under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been tried and convicted outside Canada in respect of the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the trial outside Canada the person was not present and was not represented by counsel acting under the person’s instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was not punished in accordance with the sentence imposed on conviction in respect of the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 607(6) the subsection bars the plea of autrefois convict` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offence is an offence in Canada by virtue of any of subsections 7(2) to (3.1) or (3.7), or an offence under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` AND `the person has been tried and convicted outside Canada in respect of the act or omission`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is alleged to have committed an act or omission outside Canada that is an offence in Canada by virtue of any of subsections 7(2) to (3.1) or (3.7), or an offence under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act, and in respect of which the person has been tried and convicted outside Canada"
        IF `at the trial outside Canada the person was not present and was not represented by counsel acting under the person’s instructions` AND `the person was not punished in accordance with the sentence imposed on conviction in respect of the act or omission` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not plead autrefois convict with respect to a count that charges that offence if (a) at the trial outside Canada the person was not present ..., and (b) the person was not punished" (the "if" fails) [M-a]

§ `Section 608 -- Evidence of identity of charges`

-- src:12855 | 608 Where an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried, the evidence and adjudication and the notes of the judge and official stenographer on the former trial and the record transmitted to the court pursuant to section 551 on the charge that is pending before that court are admissible in evidence to prove or to disprove the identity of the charges.
@ref s 608 (src:12855-12855)
DECLARE `s 608 the material` IS ONE OF
    `s 608 the evidence and adjudication on the former trial`
    `s 608 the notes of the judge and official stenographer on the former trial`
    `s 608 the record transmitted to the court under section 551 on the charge that is pending`
    `s 608 some other material`

-- src:12855 | 608 Where an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried, the evidence and adjudication and the notes of the judge and official stenographer on the former trial and the record transmitted to the court pursuant to section 551 on the charge that is pending before that court are admissible in evidence to prove or to disprove the identity of the charges.
@ref s 608 (src:12855-12855)
GIVEN `an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried` IS A BOOLEAN
      material IS A `s 608 the material`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 608 the material is admissible in evidence to prove or to disprove the identity of the charges` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried, the evidence and adjudication and the notes ... are admissible in evidence" [M-a]
        IF material EQUALS `s 608 some other material` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the evidence and adjudication and the notes of the judge and official stenographer on the former trial and the record transmitted to the court pursuant to section 551"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 609 -- What determines identity`

-- src:12857 | 609 (1) Where an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict to a count is tried and it appears
-- src:12858 | (a) that the matter on which the accused was given in charge on the former trial is the same in whole or in part as that on which it is proposed to give him in charge, and
-- src:12859 | (b) that on the former trial, if all proper amendments had been made that might then have been made, he might have been convicted of all the offences of which he may be convicted on the count to which the plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is pleaded,
-- src:12860 | the judge shall give judgment discharging the accused in respect of that count.
@ref s 609(1) (src:12857-12860)
GIVEN `an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict to a count is tried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that the matter on which the accused was given in charge on the former trial is the same in whole or in part as that on which it is proposed to give them in charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that on the former trial, if all proper amendments had been made that might then have been made, the accused might have been convicted of all the offences of which they may be convicted on the count to which the plea is pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 609(1) the judge must give judgment discharging the accused in respect of the count` MEANS
    IF     `an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict to a count is tried`
       AND `it appears that the matter on which the accused was given in charge on the former trial is the same in whole or in part as that on which it is proposed to give them in charge`
       AND `it appears that on the former trial, if all proper amendments had been made that might then have been made, the accused might have been convicted of all the offences of which they may be convicted on the count to which the plea is pleaded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict to a count is tried and it appears (a) ... and (b) ..., the judge shall give judgment discharging the accused in respect of that count" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12862 | (2) The following provisions apply where an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried:
-- src:12863 | (a) where it appears that the accused might on the former trial have been convicted of an offence of which he may be convicted on the count in issue, the judge shall direct that the accused shall not be found guilty of any offence of which he might have been convicted on the former trial; and
-- src:12864 | (b) where it appears that the accused may be convicted on the count in issue of an offence of which he could not have been convicted on the former trial, the accused shall plead guilty or not guilty with respect to that offence.
@ref s 609(2) (src:12862-12864)
GIVEN `an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that the accused might on the former trial have been convicted of an offence of which they may be convicted on the count in issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 609(2)(a) the judge must direct that the accused shall not be found guilty of any offence of which they might have been convicted on the former trial` MEANS
    IF `an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried` AND `it appears that the accused might on the former trial have been convicted of an offence of which they may be convicted on the count in issue`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it appears that the accused might on the former trial have been convicted of an offence of which he may be convicted on the count in issue, the judge shall direct" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12862 | (2) The following provisions apply where an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried:
-- src:12863 | (a) where it appears that the accused might on the former trial have been convicted of an offence of which he may be convicted on the count in issue, the judge shall direct that the accused shall not be found guilty of any offence of which he might have been convicted on the former trial; and
-- src:12864 | (b) where it appears that the accused may be convicted on the count in issue of an offence of which he could not have been convicted on the former trial, the accused shall plead guilty or not guilty with respect to that offence.
@ref s 609(2) (src:12862-12864)
GIVEN `an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears that the accused may be convicted on the count in issue of an offence of which they could not have been convicted on the former trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 609(2)(b) the accused must plead guilty or not guilty with respect to that offence` MEANS
    IF `an issue on a plea of autrefois acquit or autrefois convict is tried` AND `it appears that the accused may be convicted on the count in issue of an offence of which they could not have been convicted on the former trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it appears that the accused may be convicted on the count in issue of an offence of which he could not have been convicted on the former trial, the accused shall plead guilty or not guilty with respect to that offence" [M-a] [F:duty]

§ `Section 610 -- Circumstances of aggravation; murder, manslaughter and infanticide`

-- (1), the BAR: JUST TRUE where the previous conviction or acquittal bars the subsequent indictment.
-- src:12866 | 610 (1) Where an indictment charges substantially the same offence as that charged in an indictment on which an accused was previously convicted or acquitted, but adds a statement of intention or circumstances of aggravation tending, if proved, to increase the punishment, the previous conviction or acquittal bars the subsequent indictment.
@ref s 610(1) (src:12866-12866)
GIVEN `the indictment charges substantially the same offence as that charged in an indictment on which the accused was previously convicted or acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indictment adds a statement of intention or circumstances of aggravation tending, if proved, to increase the punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(1) the previous conviction or acquittal bars the subsequent indictment` MEANS
    IF `the indictment charges substantially the same offence as that charged in an indictment on which the accused was previously convicted or acquitted` AND `the indictment adds a statement of intention or circumstances of aggravation tending, if proved, to increase the punishment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an indictment charges substantially the same offence as that charged in an indictment on which an accused was previously convicted or acquitted, but adds a statement of intention or circumstances of aggravation" (the "Where" fails) [M-a]

-- (2) to (4): the bar between the kinds of homicide the core names. The core has no constructor for "murder" without a degree: murder is first degree murder or second degree murder.
-- src:12868 | (2) A conviction or an acquittal on an indictment for murder bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter or infanticide, and a conviction or acquittal on an indictment for manslaughter or infanticide bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as murder.
@ref s 610(2) (src:12868-12868)
GIVEN `the previous indictment charged` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `the subsequent indictment charges` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `there was a conviction or an acquittal on the previous indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent indictment is for the same homicide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(2) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, infanticide or murder` MEANS
    IF     `there was a conviction or an acquittal on the previous indictment` AND `the subsequent indictment is for the same homicide`
       AND (   ((`the previous indictment charged` EQUALS `first degree murder` OR `the previous indictment charged` EQUALS `second degree murder`) AND (`the subsequent indictment charges` EQUALS `manslaughter` OR `the subsequent indictment charges` EQUALS `infanticide`))
            OR ((`the previous indictment charged` EQUALS `manslaughter` OR `the previous indictment charged` EQUALS `infanticide`) AND (`the subsequent indictment charges` EQUALS `first degree murder` OR `the subsequent indictment charges` EQUALS `second degree murder`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A conviction or an acquittal on an indictment for murder bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter or infanticide, and a conviction or acquittal on an indictment for manslaughter or infanticide bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as murder"

-- src:12870 | (3) A conviction or an acquittal on an indictment for first degree murder bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as second degree murder, and a conviction or acquittal on an indictment for second degree murder bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as first degree murder.
@ref s 610(3) (src:12870-12870)
GIVEN `the previous indictment charged` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `the subsequent indictment charges` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `there was a conviction or an acquittal on the previous indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent indictment is for the same homicide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(3) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as the other degree of murder` MEANS
    IF     `there was a conviction or an acquittal on the previous indictment` AND `the subsequent indictment is for the same homicide`
       AND (   (`the previous indictment charged` EQUALS `first degree murder` AND `the subsequent indictment charges` EQUALS `second degree murder`)
            OR (`the previous indictment charged` EQUALS `second degree murder` AND `the subsequent indictment charges` EQUALS `first degree murder`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A conviction or an acquittal on an indictment for first degree murder bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as second degree murder, and a conviction or acquittal on an indictment for second degree murder bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as first degree murder"

-- src:12872 | (4) A conviction or an acquittal on an indictment for infanticide bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, and a conviction or acquittal on an indictment for manslaughter bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as infanticide.
@ref s 610(4) (src:12872-12872)
GIVEN `the previous indictment charged` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `the subsequent indictment charges` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `there was a conviction or an acquittal on the previous indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent indictment is for the same homicide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 610(4) the previous conviction or acquittal bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter or infanticide` MEANS
    IF     `there was a conviction or an acquittal on the previous indictment` AND `the subsequent indictment is for the same homicide`
       AND (   (`the previous indictment charged` EQUALS `infanticide` AND `the subsequent indictment charges` EQUALS `manslaughter`)
            OR (`the previous indictment charged` EQUALS `manslaughter` AND `the subsequent indictment charges` EQUALS `infanticide`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A conviction or an acquittal on an indictment for infanticide bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as manslaughter, and a conviction or acquittal on an indictment for manslaughter bars a subsequent indictment for the same homicide charging it as infanticide"

§ `Section 611 -- Libel, plea of justification`

-- src:12874 | 611 (1) An accused who is charged with publishing a defamatory libel may plead that the defamatory matter published by him was true, and that it was for the public benefit that the matter should have been published in the manner in which and at the time when it was published.
@ref s 611(1) (src:12874-12874)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with publishing a defamatory libel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plea is that the defamatory matter published by the accused was true, and that it was for the public benefit that the matter should have been published in the manner in which and at the time when it was published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 611(1) the accused may plead justification` MEANS
    IF `the accused is charged with publishing a defamatory libel` AND `the plea is that the defamatory matter published by the accused was true, and that it was for the public benefit that the matter should have been published in the manner in which and at the time when it was published`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who is charged with publishing a defamatory libel may plead that the defamatory matter published by him was true, and that it was for the public benefit"

-- src:12876 | (2) A plea that is made under subsection (1) may justify the defamatory matter in any sense in which it is specified in the count, or in the sense that the defamatory matter bears without being specified, or separate pleas justifying the defamatory matter in each sense may be pleaded separately to each count as if two libels had been charged in separate counts.
@ref s 611(2) (src:12876-12876)
DECLARE `s 611(2) the sense` IS ONE OF
    `s 611(2) a sense in which the defamatory matter is specified in the count`
    `s 611(2) the sense that the defamatory matter bears without being specified`
    `s 611(2) separate pleas justifying the defamatory matter in each sense, pleaded separately to each count as if two libels had been charged in separate counts`
    `s 611(2) some other sense`

-- src:12876 | (2) A plea that is made under subsection (1) may justify the defamatory matter in any sense in which it is specified in the count, or in the sense that the defamatory matter bears without being specified, or separate pleas justifying the defamatory matter in each sense may be pleaded separately to each count as if two libels had been charged in separate counts.
@ref s 611(2) (src:12876-12876)
GIVEN `a plea is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      sense IS A `s 611(2) the sense`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 611(2) the plea may justify the defamatory matter in that sense` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a plea is made under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A plea that is made under subsection (1) may justify"
        IF sense EQUALS `s 611(2) some other sense` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "in any sense in which it is specified in the count, or in the sense that the defamatory matter bears without being specified, or separate pleas"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12878 | (3) A plea that is made under subsection (1) shall be in writing and shall set out the particular facts by reason of which it is alleged to have been for the public good that the matter should have been published.
@ref s 611(3) (src:12878-12878)
GIVEN `a plea is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plea is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plea sets out the particular facts by reason of which it is alleged to have been for the public good that the matter should have been published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 611(3) the plea is in the form subsection (3) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a plea is made under subsection (1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A plea that is made under subsection (1)"
        IF `the plea is in writing` AND `the plea sets out the particular facts by reason of which it is alleged to have been for the public good that the matter should have been published` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be in writing and shall set out the particular facts by reason of which it is alleged to have been for the public good" [M-a] [F:duty]

-- src:12880 | (4) The prosecutor may in his reply deny generally the truth of a plea that is made under this section.
@ref s 611(4) (src:12880-12880)
GIVEN `a plea is made under section 611` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 611(4) the prosecutor may in the reply deny generally the truth of the plea` MEANS
    IF `a plea is made under section 611`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a plea that is made under this section"

§ `Section 612 -- Plea of justification necessary`

-- (1), the BAR: JUST TRUE where the section bars inquiring into the truth of the matters charged.
-- src:12882 | 612 (1) The truth of the matters charged in an alleged libel shall not be inquired into in the absence of a plea of justification under section 611 unless the accused is charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false, in which case evidence of the truth may be given to negative the allegation that the accused knew that the libel was false.
@ref s 612(1) (src:12882-12882)
GIVEN `there is a plea of justification under section 611` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(1) the section bars inquiring into the truth of the matters charged in the alleged libel` MEANS
    IF `there is a plea of justification under section 611` OR `the accused is charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be inquired into in the absence of a plea of justification under section 611 unless the accused is charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false" [F:unless] [M-a]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:12882 | 612 (1) The truth of the matters charged in an alleged libel shall not be inquired into in the absence of a plea of justification under section 611 unless the accused is charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false, in which case evidence of the truth may be given to negative the allegation that the accused knew that the libel was false.
@ref s 612(1) (src:12882-12882)
GIVEN `the accused is charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(1) evidence of the truth may be given to negative the allegation that the accused knew that the libel was false` MEANS
    IF `the accused is charged with publishing the libel knowing it to be false`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which case evidence of the truth may be given to negative the allegation that the accused knew that the libel was false"

-- src:12884 | (2) The accused may, in addition to a plea that is made under section 611, plead not guilty and the pleas shall be inquired into together.
@ref s 612(2) (src:12884-12884)
GIVEN `the accused makes a plea under section 611` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(2) the accused may also plead not guilty and the pleas are inquired into together` MEANS
    IF `the accused makes a plea under section 611`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in addition to a plea that is made under section 611"

-- src:12886 | (3) Where a plea of justification is pleaded and the accused is convicted, the court may, in pronouncing sentence, consider whether the guilt of the accused is aggravated or mitigated by the plea.
@ref s 612(3) (src:12886-12886)
GIVEN `a plea of justification is pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 612(3) the court may consider in pronouncing sentence whether the guilt of the accused is aggravated or mitigated by the plea` MEANS
    IF `a plea of justification is pleaded` AND `the accused is convicted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a plea of justification is pleaded and the accused is convicted, the court may, in pronouncing sentence, consider" [F:may-where] [M-a]

§ `Section 613 -- Plea of not guilty`

-- src:12888 | 613 Any ground of defence for which a special plea is not provided by this Act may be relied on under the plea of not guilty.
@ref s 613 (src:12888-12888)
GIVEN `a special plea is provided by this Act for the ground of defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 613 the ground of defence may be relied on under the plea of not guilty` MEANS
    IF `a special plea is provided by this Act for the ground of defence`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any ground of defence for which a special plea is not provided by this Act"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:12889 | 614 to 619 [ Repealed, 1991, c. 43, s. 3]
@ref s 614 to 619 (repealed) (src:12889-12889)
`s 614 to 619 what the text shows` MEANS "[ Repealed, 1991, c. 43, s. 3]"
